    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Brian Gleeson Property are delighted to present to the open market, a rare opportunity to purchase a magical apartment in the bustling town of Dungarvan, County Waterford.\r\n\r\nThis ground-floor apartment comprises a welcoming entrance hall, leading into a bright and spacious open-plan kitchen, dining and living area. The living space opens directly onto an outdoor balcony overlooking the sea; the perfect spot for alfresco dining, relaxing and watching the boats sail into Dungarvan Harbour on a warm summer’s evening.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation is completed by a generous master bedroom with ensuite, along with a separate utility room, creating a comfortable and well-appointed home.\r\n\r\nLocated in the heart of Dungarvan, this property is a real town gem, suitable for a weekend residence, retirement home, or for the professional who aspires to own their own pad in this vibrant town. With an allocated car parking space, this is a must-see home as opportunities such as this are scarce in Dungarvan.\r\n\r\nThe property is located within a stroll of Dungarvan Harbour and numerous award-winning restaurants, bars and shops. Dungarvan is a gateway to the Waterford Greenway, a spectacular 46-kilometer cycling and walking trail that follows the route of an old railway line. The Greenway passes through scenic landscapes, providing residents and tourists with a delightful outdoor experience. The town hosts various festivals and events throughout the year, including the West Waterford Festival of Food, which celebrates local culinary delights.\r\n\r\nDungarvan is a town that seamlessly blends its rich history, coastal beauty, and vibrant community spirit. Whether you're interested in exploring historical sites, enjoying outdoor activities, or immersing yourself in local culture, Dungarvan offers a delightful experience for its residents.\r\n\r\nEnjoy the pictorial essay and we look forward to showing you this immaculate home."
      },
